  "id": "Compound::DB00175 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Pravastatin is shown to interact with multiple cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzymes, including Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a5, through binding interactions. These interactions are linked to enzymatic activities that involve the oxidation of substrates, such as quinones and aromatic compounds. The CYP enzymes, in turn, are implicated in the metabolic activation of various substrates, including those that are substrates for Cyp3a4. This suggests that Pravastatin may influence Cyp3a4 through its interaction with other CYP enzymes, which in turn modulate the activity of Cyp3a4. The evidence indicates a potential mechanism by which Pravastatin could affect Cyp3a4, though the direct interaction between Pravastatin and Cyp3a4 remains unobserved in the provided data. The observed pathways highlight a network of CYP-mediated metabolic processes that could be affected by Pravastatin, supporting a mechanistic link between the drug and Cyp3a4.",
